      "id": "s11",
      "short": "Recap",
      "title": "Recap",
      "chapter": "recap",
      "body": "• A **leader** takes writes and streams them to **followers**.\n• Followers **scale reads** and survive losing a machine.\n• Async replicas **lag**: route a user’s reads to the leader right after they write.\n• When the leader dies, **fail over** to a follower.\n• Keep heavy **analytics** on its own replica.\n• Replicas are **not backups**: keep snapshots and rehearse restoring them.",
      "callout": {
        "kind": "tip",
        "text": "Next up: **Sharding** — for when even the leader can’t keep up with the writes."
      },
